  abstract     = {Maximal Abelian Extensions Unramified Outside S. Discussion and computation of the maximal abelian extension $K_S^{\text{ab}}$ of a number field $K$ unramified outside a finite set of places $S$. For a singleton prime $S = \{p\}$, $K_S^{\text{ab}}$ is given by the direct limit of ray class fields modulo $\mathfrak{p}^n \mathcal{O}_K$. Explains ramification at infinite places and the Galois group $G_S(K)^{\text{ab}} = G_S(K) / \overline{[G_S(K), G_S(K)]}$. Details the connection to class field theory, Poitou–Tate duality, and the Kronecker–Weber theorem for $K = \mathbb{Q}$.}
}

