@misc{comprehensiveglossaryalgebraic,
  title        = {{Comprehensive Glossary of Algebraic Geometry}},
  key          = {Comprehensive Glossary of Algebraic Geometry},
  url          = {https://c-keyes.github.io/files/definitions.pdf},
  howpublished = {\url{https://c-keyes.github.io/files/definitions.pdf}},
  keywords     = {math.AG, math.CT, mathematics, algebraic-geometry, sheaf-theory, category-theory, schemes, sheaf-cohomology, homological-algebra, github},
  abstract     = {Comprehensive Glossary of Algebraic Geometry. A 46-page reference dictionary compiling core definitions and theorems: - **Abelian Categories \& Additivity:** Categories equipped with biproducts $\bigoplus$, kernels, cokernels, and the first isomorphism theorem $\operatorname{Coim}(f) \cong \operatorname{Im}(f)$. Semiadditive categories satisfy $\coprod \cong \prod$, yielding semiring structures on endomorphism sets $\operatorname{End}(X)$. - **Ampleness \& Positivity:** A line bundle $\mathcal{L}$ on a projective scheme $X$ is very ample if it admits a closed immersion $X \hookrightarrow \mathbb{P}_A^n$ defined by global sections; ample if $\mathcal{L}^{\otimes m}$ is very ample for some $m > 0$. Base-point freeness means global sections generate the stalks $\mathcal{L}_x$ everywhere. - **Divisors \& Canonical Sheaves:** Cartier divisors are global sections of $\mathcal{K}_X^\times / \mathcal{O}_X^\times$. Weil divisors $\sum n_i Y_i$ are formal integer linear combinations of codimension-1 prime subvarieties. The canonical bundle $\omega_X = \det(\Omega_{X/k}^1)$ is the top exterior power of Kähler differentials, acting as the dualizing sheaf in Serre duality. - **Morphisms \& Flatness:** Flat morphisms preserve exact sequences under tensor products $\mathcal{F} \otimes_{\mathcal{O}_Y} \mathcal{O}_X$, ensuring constant Hilbert polynomials across fibers. Étale morphisms are smooth of relative dimension 0 (flat and unramified). Proper morphisms are separated, finite type, and universally closed. - **Cohomology \& Derived Functors:** Sheaf cohomology groups $H^i(X, \mathcal{F}) = R^i\Gamma(X, \mathcal{F})$ quantify obstructions to gluing local sections into global ones. Flasque and soft sheaves are acyclic, computing Čech cohomology without higher derived corrections.}
}

