  abstract     = {Noncommutative Geometry and Fundamental Physics. Alain Connes' landmark survey detailing: - **Quantum Variables:** Real variables correspond to self-adjoint operators in Hilbert space; infinitesimals correspond to compact operators. - **Metric Structures:** Distance formula $d(p, q) = \sup \{|f(p) - f(q)| : \|[D, f]\| \le 1\}$, where the line element $ds = D^{-1}$ is the fermion propagator. - **Thermodynamics \& Time:** Noncommutativity implies a canonical 1-parameter automorphism group $\delta_t \in \operatorname{Out}(\mathcal{A})$ via the Tomita–Takesaki KMS condition. - **Bost-Connes System:** Exhibits spontaneous symmetry breaking at critical temperature $\beta = 1$ with the Riemann zeta function $\zeta(\beta)$ as the partition function.}
}

