  abstract     = {Michael Harris (joint with Wee Teck Gan and Will Sawin), purity and globalization force ramification of Genestier--Lafforgue parameters of supercuspidal representations over local function fields. Key computation: for $F=k((t))$, a pure supercuspidal $\pi$ compactly induced from $U=G(\mathcal{O}_F)$ is globalized over $K=k(t)$ by the Poincaré series $P_\phi(g)=\sum_{\gamma\in G(K)}\phi(\gamma g)$ with $\phi_z=\phi_\pi$ for $z\in\mathbb{G}_m(k)$, $\phi_x=1_{G(\mathcal{O}_x)}$ off $|\mathbb{P}^1(k)|$, $\phi_\infty=1_{I_{\infty,+}}$, and $\phi_0=\chi_k$, whose support gives $P_\phi(1)=1$; if $L(\pi)$ were unramified, purity would extend $L(\Pi)_\sigma$ to a punctually pure tame local system on $\mathbb{G}_m$, hence a sum of finite-order tame characters, contradicting variation of $\chi_k$, so $L(\pi)$ is ramified and, for induction from a sufficiently small compact, wildly ramified.}
