  abstract     = {Markus J. Pflaum (joint with Hessel Posthuma and Xiang Tang), Hochschild homology of a proper Lie-groupoid convolution algebra localizes to its orbit space and, for compact actions, is computed from differential forms on fixed-point loci and the inertia space. Key computation: for the convolution sheaf $\mathcal A$ on $X=M/G$, diagonal cutoff chain maps $\Psi_{k,\varepsilon}(x_0,\ldots,x_k)=\prod_{j=0}^k\rho_\varepsilon(d^2(x_j,x_{j+1}))$ admit homotopies $bH_{k,\varepsilon}+H_{k-1,\varepsilon}b=1-\Psi_\varepsilon$, proving $HH_*(\mathcal A(X))\simeq\Gamma(X;\mathcal{HH}_*(\mathcal A))$; each stalk reduces to $C^\infty(G_x\ltimes N_x\mathcal O)$, and the twisted Connes--HKR complex $(\Omega^*(V),\iota_{Y_h})$ for $Y_h(v)=v-hv$ is quasi-isomorphic via restriction and projection to $(\Omega^*(V^h),0)$, hence $H_k(C^\infty(V),{}_hC^\infty(V))\simeq\Omega^k(V^h)$ and verifies Brylinski's inertia-form model for circle actions.}
