  keywords     = {math.OA, mathematics, operator-algebras},
  abstract     = {Adam Humeniuk, the $C^*$-covers of a nonselfadjoint operator algebra form a complete lattice, and explicit constructions separate five natural notions of equality of cover data. Key computation: ordering covers by $(C,\iota)\geq(D,\eta)$ when a surjective $*$-homomorphism $C\twoheadrightarrow D$ intertwines $\iota$ and $\eta$ makes $C^*\!\operatorname{-Lat}(A)$ a complete lattice with extrema $C^*_{\max}(A)$ and $C^*_{\mathrm{env}}(A)$; the formulas $C^*\!\operatorname{-Lat}(A\oplus B)\cong C^*\!\operatorname{-Lat}(A)\times C^*\!\operatorname{-Lat}(B)$ and, for nuclear simple $B$, $C^*\!\operatorname{-Lat}(A\otimes B)\cong C^*\!\operatorname{-Lat}(A)\otimes B$ yield examples such as $T_2$ and $T_2\otimes M_2\cong M_2(T_2)$ that are lattice-isomorphic but not lattice-intertwined, proving that isomorphism, intertwining, lattice $*$-isomorphism, lattice isomorphism, and cover equivalence are genuinely distinct.}
}

