  keywords     = {math.KT, math.CA, math.CO, math.DG, mathematics, combinatorics, harmonic-analysis, index-theory, k-theory},
  abstract     = {Guoliang Yu, localization-algebra representatives refine higher indices to secondary rho invariants whose delocalized cyclic pairings recover Lott eta invariants. Key computation: partitions of unity on covers with mesh $<1/n$ localize $F=D(1+D^2)^{-1/2}$ to $F_n=\sum_k\sqrt{\phi_k^{(n)}}F\sqrt{\phi_k^{(n)}}$, and interpolation gives $\operatorname{propagation}(F_t)\to0$, defining $\operatorname{Index}_L(D)=[\exp(2\pi i(F_\bullet+1)/2)]\in K_1(C_L^*(\widetilde X)^G)$ with $e_*\operatorname{Index}_L(D)=\operatorname{Index}(D)$; when $D$ is invertible, splicing a trivialization to this path gives $\rho(D)\in K_*(C_{L,0}^*(\widetilde X)^G)$, and for a polynomial-growth conjugacy class $\langle h\rangle$, the explicit pairing $\tau_h(u)=(2\pi i)^{-1}\int_0^\infty\operatorname{tr}_h(\dot u(t)u(t)^{-1})dt$ satisfies $\tau_h(\rho(D))=\tfrac12\eta_{\langle h\rangle}(D)$.}
}

