  abstract     = {Paolo Piazza (joint work with Hessel Posthuma, Yanli Song, and Xiang Tang), cyclic cocycles on Harish--Chandra Schwartz algebras give delocalized Atiyah--Patodi--Singer formulas for cocompact proper actions of real reductive groups. Key computation: the Connes--Moscovici heat projector $V(D)$ has entries in $\mathcal A_G^\infty(Y)$ and defines $\operatorname{Ind}_\infty(D)$; extending the semisimple orbital integral $\tau_g(f)=\int_{G/Z_G(g)}f(xgx^{-1})d(xZ_G(g))$ and applying Melrose's defect formula ${}^b\!\operatorname{Tr}[R,T]=(i/2\pi)\int_{\mathbb R}\operatorname{Tr}(\partial_\lambda I(R,\lambda)I(T,\lambda))d\lambda$ produces a relative cyclic cocycle, whose pairing yields $\langle\operatorname{Ind}_\infty(D),\tau_g^Y\rangle=\int_{Y_0^g}c^g\operatorname{AS}_g(Y_0)-\tfrac12\eta_g(D_{\partial Y})$ with $\eta_g(D)=(1/\sqrt\pi)\int_0^\infty\tau_g(D e^{-tD^2})dt/\sqrt t$.}
