  abstract     = {Masoud Khalkhali, stable anti-Yetter--Drinfeld modules supply the coefficient objects that turn Hopf symmetries into cyclic modules and recover the Connes--Moscovici theory. Key computation: for a left $H$-module coalgebra $C$ and a right-left SAYD module $M$, the complex $C^n(C,M)=M\otimes_HC^{\otimes(n+1)}$ has cyclic operator $\tau_n(m\otimes c_0\otimes\cdots\otimes c_n)=m_{(0)}\otimes c_1\otimes\cdots\otimes c_n\otimes m_{(-1)}c_0$; the anti-Yetter--Drinfeld condition makes this operator descend through $\otimes_H$, and stability gives $\tau_n^{n+1}=\operatorname{id}$, hence a cocyclic module; modular pairs in involution $(\delta,\sigma)$ are exactly one-dimensional SAYD modules ${}^\sigma\mathbb C_\delta$, so taking $C=H$ recovers Connes--Moscovici Hopf cyclic cohomology and its characteristic map $\chi_\tau(h_1\otimes\cdots\otimes h_n)(a_0,\ldots,a_n)=\tau(a_0h_1(a_1)\cdots h_n(a_n))$.}
