  abstract     = {Joachim Cuntz (joint with Guillermo Corti\~nas, Ralf Meyer, and Georg Tamme), the Feigin--Tsygan theorem identifies periodic cyclic homology of any finite-type commutative algebra in characteristic zero with the de Rham cohomology of a smooth formal presentation. Key computation: for a smooth surjection $P\twoheadrightarrow A=P/J$ and the $J$-adic completion $P_J=\varprojlim_nP/J^n$, flatness of $P_J$ over the Noetherian ring $P$ and two completed bar resolutions give a quasi-isomorphism $P_J\otimes_P(C(P),b)\to(C(P_J),b)$ and therefore $HH_*(P_J)\cong P_J\otimes_PHH_*(P)\cong P_J\otimes_P\Omega_P^*$ by HKR; under this identification Connes' $B$ becomes $d$, while nilpotent invariance gives $HP_*(A)\cong HP_*(P_J)$, hence $HP_*(A)\cong HP_*(P_J)\cong H^*_{\mathrm{dR}}(P_J)=H^*_{\mathrm{inf}}(A)$.}
