  abstract     = {Victor Nistor, localization at conjugacy classes computes cyclic invariants of crossed products and reduces the periodic cyclic homology of a real algebraic group action to its maximal compact subgroup. Key computation: for a discrete action, the condition $\gamma_0\cdots\gamma_k\in\langle\gamma\rangle$ is preserved by Hochschild faces and cyclic permutation, giving $HH_k(A\rtimes\Gamma)\cong\bigoplus_{\langle\gamma\rangle}HH_k(A\rtimes\Gamma)_\gamma$ and $HH_*(A\rtimes\Gamma)_\gamma\cong HH_*(A\rtimes\Gamma)_{\mathfrak m_\gamma}$ for $\mathfrak m_\gamma=\{f\in C^\infty(\Gamma)^\Gamma:f(\gamma)=0\}$; for a connected real algebraic $G$ with maximal compact $K$ and $q=\dim(G/K)$, localization of the smooth convolution algebra then gives $HP_*(A\rtimes G)_{\mathfrak m}\cong HP_{*+q}(A\rtimes K)_{\mathfrak m}$, so every non-elliptic localization vanishes, while $HH_*(C^\infty(K))=C^\infty(K)^K$ and $HP_*(C^\infty(K))\cong C^\infty(K)^K\otimes\mathbb C[\sigma]$ with $|\sigma|=2$.}
}

@misc{katiaconsanijoint,
