  abstract     = {Rapha\'el Ponge, measurable weak-trace-class operators are exactly Tauberian operators, giving a purely spectral formula for Connes' noncommutative integral and a semiclassical Weyl law for $L\log L$ potentials. Key computation: for $T\in\mathcal L_{1,\infty}$, $\tau(T)=[\{(\log N)^{-1}\sum_{k<N}\lambda_k(T)\}_N]\in\ell_\infty/c_0$ and every Dixmier trace is $\operatorname{Tr}_\omega=\omega\circ\tau$; independence of $\omega$ is equivalent to existence of $\lim_{N\to\infty}(\log N)^{-1}\sum_{k<N}\lambda_k(T)$, which equals $\mathop{\rlap{-}\!\int}T$; if $\int_M|V|\log(1+|V|)\,d\operatorname{vol}_g<\infty$, then $\Delta_g^{-n/4}V\Delta_g^{-n/4}\in\mathcal L_{1,\infty}$ and $\lim_{k\to\infty}k\lambda_k^\pm=c_n\int_MV_\pm\,d\operatorname{vol}_g$, hence $\mathop{\rlap{-}\!\int}\Delta_g^{-n/4}V\Delta_g^{-n/4}=c_n\int_MV\,d\operatorname{vol}_g$ and $\lim_{h\to0^+}h^nN^-(h^n\Delta_g+V)=c_n\int_MV_-\,d\operatorname{vol}_g$.}
}

