  abstract     = {Daisuke Kishimoto (joint with Kouyemon Iriye), a triangulation of an $\mathbb F$-orientable manifold is $\mathbb F$-Golod if and only if it is $\mathbb F$-tight. Key computation: the dga $C^*(K)$ with $C^p(K)=\bigoplus_{\varnothing\ne I\subset[m]}\widetilde C^{p-|I|-1}(K_I)$ is homotopy equivalent to the Koszul complex of $\mathbb F[K]$; tightness lifts cocycles from $\widetilde C^*(K_I)$ to $\widetilde C^*(K)$, and higher prism operators $P_H$ obey $\partial P_H+(-1)^{q-1}P_H\partial=\sum_{i=0}^q(-1)^iP_{H\circ(1\otimes d^i)}$, furnishing the higher homotopies that kill every product and Massey product in $H^*(C^*(K))\cong\operatorname{Tor}^S(\mathbb F[K],\mathbb F)$.}
}

