  abstract     = {Xin Fu (joint with Tseleung So, Jongbaek Song, and Stephen Theriault), the integral cohomology ring determines the away-from-small-primes homotopy type of quasitoric manifolds over products of equal-dimensional simplices. Key computation: if $M,N$ are $2n$-manifolds over $\prod_{i=1}^{\ell}\Delta^d$ and $H^*(M)\cong H^*(N)$, the fibration $\prod_{i=1}^{\ell}S^{2d+1}\to M\to BT^{m-n}$ gives $\operatorname{skel}_{2d}(M)\simeq\operatorname{skel}_{2d}(BT^{m-n})\simeq\operatorname{skel}_{2d}(N)$; for $k>d$, the attaching map homomorphism $g_M:H_{2k+2}(M)\to\pi_{2k+1}(\operatorname{skel}_{2k}M)$ is an isomorphism after inverting all primes $p\le n/d+1$, so induction over even skeleta yields $M\simeq N$ with those primes inverted.}
