  keywords     = {math.AG, math.CO, math.AT, mathematics, algebraic-geometry, algebraic-topology, discrete-geometry, toric-geometry},
  abstract     = {Tao Gong, the quotient of a toric variety attached to a Weyl polytope is homotopy equivalent to the toric variety attached to the quotient polytope, for every Lie type and every parabolic subgroup. Key computation: writing $X_P/W\cong(S_N\times(P\cap C))/\!\sim_{\mathrm{ed}}$ and $X_{P/W}\cong(S_N\times(P\cap C))/\!\sim$, the identity on representatives induces $\Phi:X_P/W\to X_{P/W}$; if $p\in\operatorname{relint}(H_I\cap F_J\cap C)$, then $\Phi^{-1}([t,p])\cong\bigl(S_N(\sigma_{[n],p})/S_N(\sigma_p)\bigr)/W_I\cong\bigl(\operatorname{Span}\{\alpha_i:i\in I\}/S_{P^\vee_{I,J}}\bigr)/W_I$, a locally contractible finite-affine quotient, so Smale's theorem gives $\Phi\simeq$ a homotopy equivalence; the same argument yields $X_P/W_K\simeq X_{P/W_K}$.}
}

