  abstract     = {Zhizhang Xie (joint work with Jinmin Wang and Guoliang Yu), a Fredholm index theorem for a twisted Dirac operator on a polyhedron proves Gromov's flat-corner domination theorem and hence Stoker's conjecture in every dimension. Key computation: for the boundary condition induced by $(\omega\otimes\omega)(c(e_n)\otimes c(e_n))$ and $0<\theta_{ij}(g)\le\theta_{ij}(g_0)<\pi$, the operator $D_B$ is essentially self-adjoint Fredholm with $\operatorname{Ind}(D_B)=\chi(P)=1$; locally the link operator has spectrum $\{-\tfrac12+k\pi/\alpha:k\in\mathbb Z\}$ and $|P_B|\ge\tfrac12$, while the integrated estimate $0=\int_P|D\phi|^2\ge\int_P|\nabla\phi|^2+\int_P\tfrac{\operatorname{Sc}_g}{4}|\phi|^2+\sum_i\int_{F_i}\tfrac{H_g}{2}|\phi|^2+\tfrac12\sum_{i,j}\int_{F_i\cap F_j}(\theta_{ij}(g_0)-\theta_{ij}(g))|\phi|^2$ forces flatness and equality of face and dihedral data.}
