  abstract     = {Piotr M. Hajac (joint work with Mariusz Tobolski), suitable graph and path homomorphisms make Leavitt path algebras contravariant and graph $C^*$-algebras covariant, yielding pushout-to-pullback theorems for quantum spaces. Key computation: for a proper target-bijective graph map $f:E\to F$, the induced map $\bar f^*:L_k(F)\to L_k(E)$ is explicitly $[\chi_p]\mapsto\sum_{q\in\bar f^{-1}(p)}[\chi_q]$, defining a contravariant functor; dually, for a path homomorphism satisfying the three regular-monomorphism conditions, $f_*:C^*(E)\to C^*(F)$ is $[\chi_p]\mapsto[\chi_{\bar f(p)}]$, defining a covariant $*$-functor and specializing to the stated pullback constructions for graph models of the equatorial Podle\'s quantum sphere and quantum $\mathbb{CP}^1$.}
